From 0207a55d13799afc4fb154445376a002614c1269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:11:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(post): Tormach probe goldens take #570's safe-plane
 descent

#583's Tormach probe goldens were written against the probe cycle before
#570 (#579), and the two merged two minutes apart, so probe_tormach failed
6/7 on main. The regenerated goldens rapid only to the safe plane
(Z 50 mm = 1.9685 in) and descend from there with a protected G38.3 feed,
where the stale ones rapided straight to Z 25 mm over the part. No
rapid below the safe plane remains in any of them; the o-word numbers
shift by the one added guard.

Fixes #695

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
